93152-26-037914","form":"6-K","filedAt":"2026-08-14","reportDate":"2026-03-31","cik":"0002011458","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/2011458/000149315226037914/ex99-2.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/46ea7b4405496fa75ef5b65282048abb475d4c1ed2b08f8bad96510d1152995d.bin","sha256":"46ea7b4405496fa75ef5b65282048abb475d4c1ed2b08f8bad96510d1152995d"}},{"id":"db375648322997a2b1c213c4cf0ce57cc2d3984e822db8233d690979add2094d","quote":"The Company’s principal revenue streams include:","context":"Revenue recognition (Continued)","section":"Business combination","block":135,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001493152-26-037914","form":"6-K","filedAt":"2026-08-14","reportDate":"2026-03-31","cik":"0002011458","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/2011458/000149315226037914/ex99-2.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/46ea7b4405496fa75ef5b65282048abb475d4c1ed2b08f8bad96510d1152995d.bin","sha256":"46ea7b4405496fa75ef5b65282048abb475d4c1ed2b08f8bad96510d1152995d"}},{"id":"d99b1fd345c63b0f0e56f04fe563f8feb05fb68c32245dd59ce3e21639652112","quote":"The Company enters into a distinct administrative services agreement with its customer, handling and managing routine corporate matters in return for a fixed service fee.","context":"Administrative services fees","section":"Business combination","block":137,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001493152-26-037914","form":"6-K","filedAt":"2026-08-14","reportDate":"2026-03-31","cik":"0002011458","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/2011458/000149315226037914/ex99-2.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/46ea7b4405496fa75ef5b65282048abb475d4c1ed2b08f8bad96510d1152995d.bin","sha256":"46ea7b4405496fa75ef5b65282048abb475d4c1ed2b08f8bad96510d1152995d"}},{"id":"02c419c21249eaeea6721fcabba8a8961bfb00bf61a6681bafb8e9a14aa1b10f","quote":"The Company is obligated to provide administrative services, which include handling and managing corporate documents, maintaining and updating corporate changes and registrations, providing registered offices, and filing income tax returns.","context":"The Company enters into a distinct administrative services agreement with its customer, handling and managing routine corporate matters in return for a fixed service fee.","section":"Business combination","block":138,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001493152-26-037914","form":"6-K","filedAt":"2026-08-14","reportDate":"2026-03-31","cik":"0002011458","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/2011458/000149315226037914/ex99-2.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/46ea7b4405496fa75ef5b65282048abb475d4c1ed2b08f8bad96510d1152995d.bin","sha256":"46ea7b4405496fa75ef5b65282048abb475d4c1ed2b08f8bad96510d1152995d"}},{"id":"19b086560e2bc1c1f133ffd25aa5f63a2eb3676803aaa8b2fe2cbb1008396578","quote":"The Company considers each element of the services within the contract to be distinct. Nevertheless, the Company concludes that the nature of the contract is to provide integrated administrative services over the term of the contract rather than a specific quantity of specified services. The activities in providing these services can vary significantly from day to day. However, these routine services are essential to fulfill the Company’s obligation to provide integrated administrative services. Therefore, the integrated administrative services transferred to the customer are substantially the same each month; that is, the customer receives substantially the same benefit each month.","context":"The Company is obligated to provide administrative services, which include handling and managing corporate documents, maintaining and updating corporate changes and registrations, providing registered offices, and filing income tax returns.","section":"Business combination","block":139,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001493152-26-037914","form":"6-K","filedAt":"2026-08-14","reportDate":"2026-03-31","cik":"0002011458","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/2011458/000149315226037914/ex99-2.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/46ea7b4405496fa75ef5b65282048abb475d4c1ed2b08f8bad96510d1152995d.bin","sha256":"46ea7b4405496fa75ef5b65282048abb475d4c1ed2b08f8bad96510d1152995d"}},{"id":"61aaa915295992e03e790502af6a983439e68f3476811d482c4adf11fe9c3f9f","quote":"The Company concludes that each increment of service is distinct, meets the criteria for recognizing revenue over time, and uses the same method for measuring progress. The performance obligation is satisfied over time in accordance with paragraph 606-10-25-27(a) because the customer simultaneously receives and consumes the benefits of the Company’s performance as each administrative transaction is processed. The fact that another entity would not need to re-perform the work that the Company has provided to date also demonstrates that the customer simultaneously receives and consumes the benefits as the Company performs.","context":"The Company considers each element of the services within the contract to be distinct. Nevertheless, the Company concludes that the nature of the contract is to provide integrated administrative services over the term of the contract rather than a specific quantity of specified services. The activities in providing these services can vary significantly from day to day. However, these routine services are essential to fulfill the Company’s obligation to provide integrated administrative services. Therefore, the integrated administrative services transferred to the customer are substantially the same each month; that is, the customer receives substantially the same benefit each month.","section":"Business combination","block":140,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001493152-26-037914","form":"6-K","filedAt":"2026-08-14","reportDate":"2026-03-31","cik":"0002011458","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/2011458/000149315226037914/ex99-2.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/46ea7b4405496fa75ef5b65282048abb475d4c1ed2b08f8bad96510d1152995d.bin","sha256":"46ea7b4405496fa75ef5b65282048abb475d4c1ed2b08f8bad96510d1152995d"}},{"id":"dff069d48571262e83aea233cd79cbe6f5cdb35296cd612f14d113297e23bfe1","quote":"The Company further concludes that the integrated administrative services represent a series of distinct goods or services that are substantially the same and that have the same pattern of transfer to the customers, satisfying the requirements of ASC 606-10-25-14(b) to be accounted for as a single performance obligation.","context":"The Company concludes that each increment of service is distinct, meets the criteria for recognizing revenue over time, and uses the same method for measuring progress. The performance obligation is satisfied over time in accordance with paragraph 606-10-25-27(a) because the customer simultaneously receives and consumes the benefits of the Company’s performance as each administrative transaction is processed. The fact that another entity would not need to re-perform the work that the Company has provided to date also demonstrates that the customer simultaneously receives and consumes the benefits as the Company performs.","section":"Business combination","block":141,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001493152-26-037914","form":"6-K","filedAt":"2026-08-14","reportDate":"2026-03-31","cik":"0002011458","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/2011458/000149315226037914/ex99-2.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/46ea7b4405496fa75ef5b65282048abb475d4c1ed2b08f8bad96510d1152995d.bin","sha256":"46ea7b4405496fa75ef5b65282048abb475d4c1ed2b08f8bad96510d1152995d"}},{"id":"7c0391989dc4abdb09662641c05eea0dfa1894fa15e7d27c99c88c448a4cd342","quote":"The Company promises to provide a set of integrated administrative services (stand-ready obligations) over a fixed period, with the customer having no explicit limit on the use of services within this period. The Company determines that its promise to the customer is to provide a service of making the integrated administrative work available as needed. The extent of the customers’ request for the administrative work does not affect the remaining services to which the customer is entitled. As suggested above, the Company determines that the customer benefits largely evenly from the Company’s services of making the administrative service available throughout the contract period. The integrated administrative services transferred to the customer are substantially the same during each particular month; that is, the customer receives substantially the same benefit each month. Therefore, the Company concludes that the best measure of progress toward complete satisfaction of the performance obligation over time is a time-based measure, and it recognizes revenue on a straight-line basis throughout the contract period.","context":"The Company further concludes that the integrated administrative services represent a series of distinct goods or services that are substantially the same and that have the same pattern of transfer to the customers, satisfying the requirements of ASC 606-10-25-14(b) to be accounted for as a single performance obligation.","section":"Business combination","block":142,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001493152-26-037914","form":"6-K","filedAt":"2026-08-14","reportDate":"2026-03-31","cik":"0002011458","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/2011458/000149315226037914/ex99-2.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/46ea7b4405496fa75ef5b65282048abb475d4c1ed2b08f8bad96510d1152995d.bin","sha256":"46ea7b4405496fa75ef5b65282048abb475d4c1ed2b08f8bad96510d1152995d"}},{"id":"b430c9686891dea13fbae9d192ab1db8a33c287b2d12d7114cedf7a712c23fa8","quote":"According to the agreement, the customer is required to pay a monthly fee for administrative services. In practice, the Company issues invoices to customer on a quarterly basis for these services, consolidating three months of fees into one invoice and payment is due from the date of billing. The customer pays before the end of the quarters.","context":"The Company promises to provide a set of integrated administrative services (stand-ready obligations) over a fixed period, with the customer having no explicit limit on the use of services within this period. The Company determines that its promise to the customer is to provide a service of making the integrated administrative work available as needed. The extent of the customers’ request for the administrative work does not affect the remaining services to which the customer is entitled. As suggested above, the Company determines that the customer benefits largely evenly from the Company’s services of making the administrative service available throughout the contract period. The integrated administrative services transferred to the customer are substantially the same during each particular month; that is, the customer receives substantially the same benefit each month. Therefore, the Company concludes that the best measure of progress toward complete satisfaction of the performance obligation over time is a time-based measure, and it recognizes revenue on a straight-line basis throughout the contract period.","section":"Business combination","block":143,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001493152-26-037914","form":"6-K","filedAt":"2026-08-14","reportDate":"2026-03-31","cik":"0002011458","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/2011458/000149315226037914/ex99-2.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/46ea7b4405496fa75ef5b65282048abb475d4c1ed2b08f8bad96510d1152995d.bin","sha256":"46ea7b4405496fa75ef5b65282048abb475d4c1ed2b08f8bad96510d1152995d"}},{"id":"d5ec60394750f09011ed91e9a5a1026507e312b3595a284085841f733dddea85","quote":"On July 1, 2025, the Company terminated the administrative services agreement, and no administrative services fees has been generated from July 1, 2025.","context":"According to the agreement, the customer is required to pay a monthly fee for administrative services. In practice, the Company issues invoices to customer on a quarterly basis for these services, consolidating three months of fees into one invoice and payment is due from the date of billing. The customer pays before the end of the quarters.","section":"Business combination","block":144,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001493152-26-037914","form":"6-K","filedAt":"2026-08-14","reportDate":"2026-03-31","cik":"0002011458","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/2011458/000149315226037914/ex99-2.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/46ea7b4405496fa75ef5b65282048abb475d4c1ed2b08f8bad96510d1152995d.bin","sha256":"46ea7b4405496fa75ef5b65282048abb475d4c1ed2b08f8bad96510d1152995d"}},{"id":"528d14247e4917d903354402d5dab3026276a9c9f94beaa0cfa8fe7a248b17c7","quote":"Fintech service fees – algorithm and big data","context":"On July 1, 2025, the Company terminated the administrative services agreement, and no administrative services fees has been generated from July 1, 2025.","section":"Business combination","block":145,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001493152-26-037914","form":"6-K","filedAt":"2026-08-14","reportDate":"2026-03-31","cik":"0002011458","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/2011458/000149315226037914/ex99-2.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/46ea7b4405496fa75ef5b65282048abb475d4c1ed2b08f8bad96510d1152995d.bin","sha256":"46ea7b4405496fa75ef5b65282048abb475d4c1ed2b08f8bad96510d1152995d"}},{"id":"4ffa6a602881d33ba14ee33c9345ff72009729c607fdff10924594bc42b2a76b","quote":"The Company enters into distinct fintech services agreements with its customers to provide algorithms and big data models for the customers’ use in return for a fintech service fee. There are two types of arrangement entered, i.e. (i) brokering the algorithms and big data models on behalf of the vendor and (ii) providing fintech services related to the algorithms and big data models directly to the customers.","context":"Fintech service fees – algorithm and big data","section":"Business combination","block":146,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001493152-26-037914","form":"6-K","filedAt":"2026-08-14","reportDate":"2026-03-31","cik":"0002011458","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/2011458/000149315226037914/ex99-2.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/46ea7b4405496fa75ef5b65282048abb475d4c1ed2b08f8bad96510d1152995d.bin","sha256":"46ea7b4405496fa75ef5b65282048abb475d4c1ed2b08f8bad96510d1152995d"}},{"id":"a44ce587d147c0afd4cd1cd5c82d67a627bb7d5a4ee0cc3c343e8e6b6af86332","quote":"The Company brokered the algorithms and big data models on behalf of the vendor until it acquired the related fintech solution from the vendor in August 2024. The Company enters into distinct fintech services agreements with its customer to provide algorithms and big data models developed by a vendor for the customer’s use in return for a fintech service fee.","context":"Brokering the algorithms and big data models","section":"Business combination","block":148,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001493152-26-037914","form":"6-K","filedAt":"2026-08-14","reportDate":"2026-03-31","cik":"0002011458","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/2011458/000149315226037914/ex99-2.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/46ea7b4405496fa75ef5b65282048abb475d4c1ed2b08f8bad96510d1152995d.bin","sha256":"46ea7b4405496fa75ef5b65282048abb475d4c1ed2b08f8bad96510d1152995d"}},{"id":"313cb90caea0214c3553f9250567a508962743848949e2dada59003ba7097841","quote":"The Company accounts for the fintech services related to the brokering of algorithms and big data models as a single performance obligation in accordance with ASC 606-10-25-14(b). This is because it provides a series of distinct services that are substantially the same by making the algorithms and big data models available for the customers’ use during a fixed period, and these services have the same pattern of transfer (the services transfer to the customer over time and use the same method to measure progress — that is, a time-based measure of progress).","context":"The Company brokered the algorithms and big data models on behalf of the vendor until it acquired the related fintech solution from the vendor in August 2024. The Company enters into distinct fintech services agreements with its customer to provide algorithms and big data models developed by a vendor for the customer’s use in return for a fintech service fee.","section":"Business combination","block":149,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001493152-26-037914","form":"6-K","filedAt":"2026-08-14","reportDate":"2026-03-31","cik":"0002011458","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/2011458/000149315226037914/ex99-2.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/46ea7b4405496fa75ef5b65282048abb475d4c1ed2b08f8bad96510d1152995d.bin","sha256":"46ea7b4405496fa75ef5b65282048abb475d4c1ed2b08f8bad96510d1152995d"}},{"id":"29c1f09add1693e8c6a075389b41654c4c12e158ae880fae0a8295b63645e08b","quote":"Notes to Unaudited Condensed Consolidated Financial Statements","context":"Zenta Group Company Limited","section":"Business combination","block":152,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001493152-26-037914","form":"6-K","filedAt":"2026-08-14","reportDate":"2026-03-31","cik":"0002011458","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/2011458/000149315226037914/ex99-2.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/46ea7b4405496fa75ef5b65282048abb475d4c1ed2b08f8bad96510d1152995d.bin","sha256":"46ea7b4405496fa75ef5b65282048abb475d4c1ed2b08f8bad96510d1152995d"}},{"id":"ec05616f988ac7aa0a2e1118aea6f0b0700cfacf6a3e7e3ef51a44a204693701","quote":"For the Six Months Ended March 31, 2026, 2025 and 2024","context":"Notes to Unaudited Condensed Consolidated Financial Statements","section":"Business combination","block":153,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001493152-26-037914","form":"6-K","filedAt":"2026-08-14","reportDate":"2026-03-31","cik":"0002011458","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/2011458/000149315226037914/ex99-2.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/46ea7b4405496fa75ef5b65282048abb475d4c1ed2b08f8bad96510d1152995d.bin","sha256":"46ea7b4405496fa75ef5b65282048abb475d4c1ed2b08f8bad96510d1152995d"}},{"id":"9a4dc33a9ff261db5e62de61d375e90fef65516720661969932aaffeff753ba0","quote":"3. Summary of Significant Accounting Policies (Continued)","context":"For the Six Months Ended March 31, 2026, 2025 and 2024","section":"Business combination","block":154,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001493152-26-037914","form":"6-K","filedAt":"2026-08-14","reportDate":"2026-03-31","cik":"0002011458","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/2011458/000149315226037914/ex99-2.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/46ea7b4405496fa75ef5b65282048abb475d4c1ed2b08f8bad96510d1152995d.bin","sha256":"46ea7b4405496fa75ef5b65282048abb475d4c1ed2b08f8bad96510d1152995d"}},{"id":"3224bc0730ae228f963208cc199ef7705471f40cea0a272ec654228fee6b6b57","quote":"As stated in the agreement, the pricing structure for the fintech services related to the provision of algorithms and big data models includes a fixed component based on a predetermined amount of usage (i.e., a minimum usage requirement) and a variable component that is charged if the customer exceeds the predetermined amount (i.e., “overage fees”). In addition, if the customer does not meet the minimum usage requirement in any month, the shortfall is carried over to the following month.","context":"Revenue recognition (Continued)","section":"Business combination","block":156,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001493152-26-037914","form":"6-K","filedAt":"2026-08-14","reportDate":"2026-03-31","cik":"0002011458","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/2011458/000149315226037914/ex99-2.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/46ea7b4405496fa75ef5b65282048abb475d4c1ed2b08f8bad96510d1152995d.bin","sha256":"46ea7b4405496fa75ef5b65282048abb475d4c1ed2b08f8bad96510d1152995d"}},{"id":"68d79bfd53139ad42145424b3b7d0d9e3c16a7d42eb414249be5c61791d59346","quote":"Because the minimum usage requirements can change each month and the usage-based fees are related to a specific outcome, the allocation of the variable consideration to each distinct service period (e.g., each month) cannot meet the allocation objective. This means that the usage-based pricing may not represent the amount of consideration to which the entity expects to be entitled upon the transfer of each distinct service, which is based on each increment of time within the series. Therefore, any overage fees for a particular month may not (1) be solely associated with that month or (2) reflect the value of the specific outcome associated with the overage. Accordingly, the Company does not qualify to apply the variable consideration allocation exception set out under ASC 606-10-32-40 and is required to estimate the amount of variable consideration to which it would be entitled at contract inception.","context":"As stated in the agreement, the pricing structure for the fintech services related to the provision of algorithms and big data models includes a fixed component based on a predetermined amount of usage (i.e., a minimum usage requirement) and a variable component that is charged if the customer exceeds the predetermined amount (i.e., “overage fees”). In addition, if the customer does not meet the minimum usage requirement in any month, the shortfall is carried over to the following month.","section":"Business combination","block":157,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001493152-26-037914","form":"6-K","filedAt":"2026-08-14","reportDate":"2026-03-31","cik":"0002011458","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/2011458/000149315226037914/ex99-2.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/46ea7b4405496fa75ef5b65282048abb475d4c1ed2b08f8bad96510d1152995d.bin","sha256":"46ea7b4405496fa75ef5b65282048abb475d4c1ed2b08f8bad96510d1152995d"}},{"id":"4768da0d3645251bc0bf6c9b7307e657698508871cd074ce27ad46a10ca172e1","quote":"The Company believes that the most likely amount method is the preferred method for predicting the amount of consideration to which it will be entitled. Under the most likely amount method, based on the Company’s best estimate, the Company does not expect that usage exceeding the predetermined amount will occur during the brokering services period. Therefore, the minimum usage requirement as determined in the agreement is the most likely amount that the Company would be entitled to.","context":"Because the minimum usage requirements can change each month and the usage-based fees are related to a specific outcome, the allocation of the variable consideration to each distinct service period (e.g., each month) cannot meet the allocation objective. This means that the usage-based pricing may not represent the amount of consideration to which the entity expects to be entitled upon the transfer of each distinct service, which is based on each increment of time within the series. Therefore, any overage fees for a particular month may not (1) be solely associated with that month or (2) reflect the value of the specific outcome associated with the overage. Accordingly, the Company does not qualify to apply the variable consideration allocation exception set out under ASC 606-10-32-40 and is required to estimate the amount of variable consideration to which it would be entitled at contract inception.","section":"Business combination","block":158,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001493152-26-037914","form":"6-K","filedAt":"2026-08-14","reportDate":"2026-03-31","cik":"0002011458","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/2011458/000149315226037914/ex99-2.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/46ea7b4405496fa75ef5b65282048abb475d4c1ed2b08f8bad96510d1152995d.bin","sha256":"46ea7b4405496fa75ef5b65282048abb475d4c1ed2b08f8bad96510d1152995d"}},{"id":"d7ea886d124c248873d750fc2d91aee02d7a7a32134c851a13a30904d55035cf","quote":"The Company also considers the guidance in ASC 606-10-32-11 through 32-13 on constraining estimates of variable consideration to determine whether the estimated amount of variable consideration should be included in the transaction price. The Company considers the factors in ASC 606-10-32-12 and observes that the amount of consideration is highly susceptible to factors outside the Company’s influence (that is, inherently variable depending on future customer actions, and there is no historical data to support any of the estimates). As such, it cannot conclude that it is probable that a significant reversal in the amount of cumulative revenue recognized will not occur. Consequently, the Company believes that it should not include any variable consideration in the transaction price.","context":"The Company believes that the most likely amount method is the preferred method for predicting the amount of consideration to which it will be entitled. Under the most likely amount method, based on the Company’s best estimate, the Company does not expect that usage exceeding the predetermined amount will occur during the brokering services period. Therefore, the minimum usage requirement as determined in the agreement is the most likely amount that the Company would be entitled to.","section":"Business combination","block":159,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001493152-26-037914","form":"6-K","filedAt":"2026-08-14","reportDate":"2026-03-31","cik":"0002011458","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/2011458/000149315226037914/ex99-2.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/46ea7b4405496fa75ef5b65282048abb475d4c1ed2b08f8bad96510d1152995d.bin","sha256":"46ea7b4405496fa75ef5b65282048abb475d4c1ed2b08f8bad96510d1152995d"}},{"id":"9d90f0448b238b5d59bf9518f138bab86f6bca510715b9c7a1a6cc8407bf95ca","quote":"For the algorithms and big data models brokered by the Company, customer simultaneously receives and consumes the benefits as the services are rendered by the Company, i.e., access to and utilize the models according to the customers’ needs. Because the revenue generated from brokering the algorithms and big data models meets one of the criteria set out in ASC 606-10-25-27, the revenue from brokering the algorithms and big data models qualifies to be recognized over time, with the fixed consideration (i.e., the minimum usage payment) recognized ratably across the contract period.","context":"The Company also considers the guidance in ASC 606-10-32-11 through 32-13 on constraining estimates of variable consideration to determine whether the estimated amount of variable consideration should be included in the transaction price. The Company considers the factors in ASC 606-10-32-12 and observes that the amount of consideration is highly susceptible to factors outside the Company’s influence (that is, inherently variable depending on future customer actions, and there is no historical data to support any of the estimates). As such, it cannot conclude that it is probable that a significant reversal in the amount of cumulative revenue recognized will not occur. Consequently, the Company believes that it should not include any variable consideration in the transaction price.","section":"Business combination","block":160,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001493152-26-037914","form":"6-K","filedAt":"2026-08-14","reportDate":"2026-03-31","cik":"0002011458","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/2011458/000149315226037914/ex99-2.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/46ea7b4405496fa75ef5b65282048abb475d4c1ed2b08f8bad96510d1152995d.bin","sha256":"46ea7b4405496fa75ef5b65282048abb475d4c1ed2b08f8bad96510d1152995d"}},{"id":"3f986618175b8ecdf4736cc774a3bb33bccbde7d6e6123b1996aabf8dc8df4ba","quote":"According to the agreement, the customer is required to settle the actual usage amounts on a quarterly basis and make payment within 60 days from the date signed on the usage confirmation letter, and any shortfall against the minimum usage requirement within 90 days from the end of the contract term, i.e. September 30, 2024. The customer adheres to the payment term and pays before the due date.","context":"For the algorithms and big data models brokered by the Company, customer simultaneously receives and consumes the benefits as the services are rendered by the Company, i.e., access to and utilize the models according to the customers’ needs. Because the revenue generated from brokering the algorithms and big data models meets one of the criteria set out in ASC 606-10-25-27, the revenue from brokering the algorithms and big data models qualifies to be recognized over time, with the fixed consideration (i.e., the minimum usage payment) recognized ratably across the contract period.","section":"Business combination","block":161,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001493152-26-037914","form":"6-K","filedAt":"2026-08-14","reportDate":"2026-03-31","cik":"0002011458","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/2011458/000149315226037914/ex99-2.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/46ea7b4405496fa75ef5b65282048abb475d4c1ed2b08f8bad96510d1152995d.bin","sha256":"46ea7b4405496fa75ef5b65282048abb475d4c1ed2b08f8bad96510d1152995d"}},{"id":"7d7665c1ef27ee84d4f7dbed131cae3408f2441986471f79281cc2aa760553aa","quote":"The Company follows the rules and guidance set out under ASC 606 when determining whether it is acting as a principal or an agent in the contract with its customers. The core principle of ASC 606 requires an entity to determine whether the nature of its promise is a performance obligation to provide the services itself (that is, the entity is a principal) or to arrange for those services to be provided by another party (that is, the entity is an agent). The following steps are applied to achieve that core principle:","context":"According to the agreement, the customer is required to settle the actual usage amounts on a quarterly basis and make payment within 60 days from the date signed on the usage confirmation letter, and any shortfall against the minimum usage requirement within 90 days from the end of the contract term, i.e. September 30, 2024. The customer adheres to the payment term and pays before the due date.","section":"Business combination","block":162,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001493152-26-037914","form":"6-K","filedAt":"2026-08-14","reportDate":"2026-03-31","cik":"0002011458","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/2011458/000149315226037914/ex99-2.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/46ea7b4405496fa75ef5b65282048abb475d4c1ed2b08f8bad96510d1152995d.bin","sha256":"46ea7b4405496fa75ef5b65282048abb475d4c1ed2b08f8bad96510d1152995d"}},{"id":"1d038cab58825a14b66ef3b47c66f36c5ae8477a89e247b2bece4ece3bd26da4","quote":"Step 1: Identify the specified services to be provided to the customer.","context":"The Company follows the rules and guidance set out under ASC 606 when determining whether it is acting as a principal or an agent in the contract with its customers. The core principle of ASC 606 requires an entity to determine whether the nature of its promise is a performance obligation to provide the services itself (that is, the entity is a principal) or to arrange for those services to be provided by another party (that is, the entity is an agent). The following steps are applied to achieve that core principle:","section":"Business combination","block":163,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001493152-26-037914","form":"6-K","filedAt":"2026-08-14","reportDate":"2026-03-31","cik":"0002011458","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/2011458/000149315226037914/ex99-2.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/46ea7b4405496fa75ef5b65282048abb475d4c1ed2b08f8bad96510d1152995d.bin","sha256":"46ea7b4405496fa75ef5b65282048abb475d4c1ed2b08f8bad96510d1152995d"}},{"id":"fe901ee367f4da89daa38fb0d29507e2194be768c6bd3276a475b82985d503f5","quote":"Step 2: Assess whether it controls each specified service before that service is transferred to the customer.","context":"Step 1: Identify the specified services to be provided to the customer.","section":"Business combination","block":164,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001493152-26-037914","form":"6-K","filedAt":"2026-08-14","reportDate":"2026-03-31","cik":"0002011458","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/2011458/000149315226037914/ex99-2.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/46ea7b4405496fa75ef5b65282048abb475d4c1ed2b08f8bad96510d1152995d.bin","sha256":"46ea7b4405496fa75ef5b65282048abb475d4c1ed2b08f8bad96510d1152995d"}},{"id":"e87ad46c8f7d05e00682d76992b0cf0ac5a9ac4b973e26bc76c157532b1f1830","quote":"Under the agreement the Company has in place with its customer, the Company does not have primary responsibility for providing algorithms and big data models but brokering them from a vendor. The models are primarily controlled by the vendor, who sets the transaction price or income to be shared with the Company in separate documents. The Company has no control over the models and cannot determine the transaction price set by the vendor. Furthermore, it has been stated in the agreement that the models are run by the vendor, and the Company would be indemnified by the vendor for any issues, damages, and claims related to the services. The responsibility of the Company is simply to broker the algorithms and big data models from the vendor to its customer. The Company concludes it has no primary responsibility in the function but acts as an agent between its customer and the vendor. The Company recognizes revenue at the net amount after deducting the amount it is required to pay to the vendor.","context":"Step 2: Assess whether it controls each specified service before that service is transferred to the customer.","section":"Business combination","block":165,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001493152-26-037914","form":"6-K","filedAt":"2026-08-14","reportDate":"2026-03-31","cik":"0002011458","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/2011458/000149315226037914/ex99-2.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/46ea7b4405496fa75ef5b65282048abb475d4c1ed2b08f8bad96510d1152995d.bin","sha256":"46ea7b4405496fa75ef5b65282048abb475d4c1ed2b08f8bad96510d1152995d"}},{"id":"9fe60b81f08498ba429a1824bfc1c1837ec40cb966d87a5aa2ed709283a1e58c","quote":"Providing the algorithms and big data models directly to its customers","context":"Under the agreement the Company has in place with its customer, the Company does not have primary responsibility for providing algorithms and big data models but brokering them from a vendor. The models are primarily controlled by the vendor, who sets the transaction price or income to be shared with the Company in separate documents. The Company has no control over the models and cannot determine the transaction price set by the vendor. Furthermore, it has been stated in the agreement that the models are run by the vendor, and the Company would be indemnified by the vendor for any issues, damages, and claims related to the services. The responsibility of the Company is simply to broker the algorithms and big data models from the vendor to its customer. The Company concludes it has no primary responsibility in the function but acts as an agent between its customer and the vendor. The Company recognizes revenue at the net amount after deducting the amount it is required to pay to the vendor.","section":"Business combination","block":166,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001493152-26-037914","form":"6-K","filedAt":"2026-08-14","reportDate":"2026-03-31","cik":"0002011458","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/2011458/000149315226037914/ex99-2.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/46ea7b4405496fa75ef5b65282048abb475d4c1ed2b08f8bad96510d1152995d.bin","sha256":"46ea7b4405496fa75ef5b65282048abb475d4c1ed2b08f8bad96510d1152995d"}},{"id":"15155bb9eb030bfd4d02efa978caf4d05d4f4f9fcc8204c7cfb57e17bf32b5f2","quote":"Since it acquired the related fintech solution from the vendor in August 2024, the Company provides the fintech services related to the provision of algorithms and big data models to its customers directly in return for fee income. The Company enters into distinct fintech services agreements with its customers to provide algorithms and big data models owned by the Company for the customers’ use in return for a fintech service fee.","context":"Providing the algorithms and big data models directly to its customers","section":"Business combination","block":167,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001493152-26-037914","form":"6-K","filedAt":"2026-08-14","reportDate":"2026-03-31","cik":"0002011458","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/2011458/000149315226037914/ex99-2.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/46ea7b4405496fa75ef5b65282048abb475d4c1ed2b08f8bad96510d1152995d.bin","sha256":"46ea7b4405496fa75ef5b65282048abb475d4c1ed2b08f8bad96510d1152995d"}},{"id":"fd41584fc220a26341783030ecc75005fb45a96fd71dadf152b0038a87982c66","quote":"The Company accounts for the fintech services related to provision of algorithms and big data models as a single performance obligation in accordance with ASC 606-10-25-14(b). This is because it provides a series of distinct services that are substantially the same by making the algorithms and big data models available for the customers’ use during a fixed period, and these services have the same pattern of transfer (the services transfer to the customer over time and use the same method to measure progress — that is, a time-based measure of progress).","context":"Since it acquired the related fintech solution from the vendor in August 2024, the Company provides the fintech services related to the provision of algorithms and big data models to its customers directly in return for fee income. The Company enters into distinct fintech services agreements with its customers to provide algorithms and big data models owned by the Company for the customers’ use in return for a fintech service fee.","section":"Business combination","block":168,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001493152-26-037914","form":"6-K","filedAt":"2026-08-14","reportDate":"2026-03-31","cik":"0002011458","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/2011458/000149315226037914/ex99-2.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/46ea7b4405496fa75ef5b65282048abb475d4c1ed2b08f8bad96510d1152995d.bin","sha256":"46ea7b4405496fa75ef5b65282048abb475d4c1ed2b08f8bad96510d1152995d"}},{"id":"6df12db8532ced82597a4ddc12d7f6d3549b02622aa486485ba90ee931af4682","quote":"Notes to Unaudited Condensed Consolidated Financial Statements","context":"Zenta Group Company Limited","section":"Business combination","block":171,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001493152-26-037914","form":"6-K","filedAt":"2026-08-14","reportDate":"2026-03-31","cik":"0002011458","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/2011458/000149315226037914/ex99-2.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/46ea7b4405496fa75ef5b65282048abb475d4c1ed2b08f8bad96510d1152995d.bin","sha256":"46ea7b4405496fa75ef5b65282048abb475d4c1ed2b08f8bad96510d1152995d"}},{"id":"3b3ed6ed304c5b8b659e844a9a837ea5396ab423acbcabb673e287785816f186","quote":"For the Six Months Ended March 31, 2026, 2025 and 2024","context":"Notes to Unaudited Condensed Consolidated Financial Statements","section":"Business combination","block":172,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001493152-26-037914","form":"6-K","filedAt":"2026-08-14","reportDate":"2026-03-31","cik":"0002011458","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/2011458/000149315226037914/ex99-2.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/46ea7b4405496fa75ef5b65282048abb475d4c1ed2b08f8bad96510d1152995d.bin","sha256":"46ea7b4405496fa75ef5b65282048abb475d4c1ed2b08f8bad96510d1152995d"}},{"id":"efbd1fe5bfee2ea3ea1b3e3c1d35922e7308fa26ffcb4151d215ef5d028a0883","quote":"3. Summary of Significant Accounting Policies (Continued)","context":"For the Six Months Ended March 31, 2026, 2025 and 2024","section":"Business combination","block":173,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001493152-26-037914","form":"6-K","filedAt":"2026-08-14","reportDate":"2026-03-31","cik":"0002011458","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/2011458/000149315226037914/ex99-2.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/46ea7b4405496fa75ef5b65282048abb475d4c1ed2b08f8bad96510d1152995d.bin","sha256":"46ea7b4405496fa75ef5b65282048abb475d4c1ed2b08f8bad96510d1152995d"}},{"id":"0d648c2a2d546f0f9407907164ba012431605d60068e47a450c61e45fca7f28d","quote":"For contracts enacted before the acquisition of the related fintech solution, the pricing structure for the fintech services related to the provision of algorithms and big data models includes a fixed component based on a predetermined amount of usage and a variable component as detailed under “Brokering the algorithms and big data models” above. While the Company transitioned to directly providing these fintech services to customers in exchange for fee income after acquiring the related fintech solution, it continues to honor the existing pricing structure for contracts executed prior to the acquisition until those contracts are completed.","context":"Revenue recognition (Continued)","section":"Business combination","block":175,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001493152-26-037914","form":"6-K","filedAt":"2026-08-14","reportDate":"2026-03-31","cik":"0002011458","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/2011458/000149315226037914/ex99-2.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/46ea7b4405496fa75ef5b65282048abb475d4c1ed2b08f8bad96510d1152995d.bin","sha256":"46ea7b4405496fa75ef5b65282048abb475d4c1ed2b08f8bad96510d1152995d"}},{"id":"cbbc70b7686ff50ffba0248af239ef03378d4f75dbba89037ee2896426efb2d9","quote":"For contracts enacted after the acquisition of the related fintech solution, the previous pricing structure is no longer offered. As stated in the agreement, the pricing structure for the fintech services related to the provision of algorithms and big data models is based solely on usage (i.e., the actual usage payment) during the service period. The variable consideration allocation exception is applied as (1) the usage-based fees are related to a specific outcome and (2) allocation of the variable consideration to each distinct service period (e.g. each month) would meet the allocation objective (i.e., the usage-based pricing represents the amount of consideration to which the Company expects to be entitled upon the transfer of each and every distinct service, which is based on each increment of time within the series). Accordingly, the Company is not required to estimate the amount of variable consideration to which it would be entitled at contract inception and instead can recognize revenue as the customer’s usage occurs.","context":"For contracts enacted before the acquisition of the related fintech solution, the pricing structure for the fintech services related to the provision of algorithms and big data models includes a fixed component based on a predetermined amount of usage and a variable component as detailed under “Brokering the algorithms and big data models” above. While the Company transitioned to directly providing these fintech services to customers in exchange for fee income after acquiring the related fintech solution, it continues to honor the existing pricing structure for contracts executed prior to the acquisition until those contracts are completed.","section":"Business combination","block":176,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001493152-26-037914","form":"6-K","filedAt":"2026-08-14","reportDate":"2026-03-31","cik":"0002011458","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/2011458/000149315226037914/ex99-2.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/46ea7b4405496fa75ef5b65282048abb475d4c1ed2b08f8bad96510d1152995d.bin","sha256":"46ea7b4405496fa75ef5b65282048abb475d4c1ed2b08f8bad96510d1152995d"}},{"id":"5ba4f85110cf3db29e035c738774bf36e2c28d6272c6098554978f66cfafbe00","quote":"For the algorithms and big data models provided directly by the Company to its customers, customers simultaneously receive and consume the benefits as the services are rendered by the Company, i.e., access to and utilize the models according to the customers’ needs. Because the revenue generated from provision the algorithms and big data models meets one of the criteria set out in ASC 606-10-25-27, the revenue from the provision of algorithms and big data models qualifies to be recognized over time, with the variable consideration (i.e., the actual usage payment) recognized based solely on usage during the service period.","context":"For contracts enacted after the acquisition of the related fintech solution, the previous pricing structure is no longer offered. As stated in the agreement, the pricing structure for the fintech services related to the provision of algorithms and big data models is based solely on usage (i.e., the actual usage payment) during the service period. The variable consideration allocation exception is applied as (1) the usage-based fees are related to a specific outcome and (2) allocation of the variable consideration to each distinct service period (e.g. each month) would meet the allocation objective (i.e., the usage-based pricing represents the amount of consideration to which the Company expects to be entitled upon the transfer of each and every distinct service, which is based on each increment of time within the series). Accordingly, the Company is not required to estimate the amount of variable consideration to which it would be entitled at contract inception and instead can recognize revenue as the customer’s usage occurs.","section":"Business combination","block":177,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001493152-26-037914","form":"6-K","filedAt":"2026-08-14","reportDate":"2026-03-31","cik":"0002011458","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/2011458/000149315226037914/ex99-2.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/46ea7b4405496fa75ef5b65282048abb475d4c1ed2b08f8bad96510d1152995d.bin","sha256":"46ea7b4405496fa75ef5b65282048abb475d4c1ed2b08f8bad96510d1152995d"}},{"id":"aa06691dbc3893320f517def5c3438dc840bdb7ec6ab0933fb1f3d1955a1cb81","quote":"According to the agreement, the customers are required to settle the actual usage amounts on a quarterly basis and make payment within 60 days from the date signed on the usage confirmation letter. The customer adheres to the payment term and pays before the due date.","context":"For the algorithms and big data models provided directly by the Company to its customers, customers simultaneously receive and consume the benefits as the services are rendered by the Company, i.e., access to and utilize the models according to the customers’ needs. Because the revenue generated from provision the algorithms and big data models meets one of the criteria set out in ASC 606-10-25-27, the revenue from the provision of algorithms and big data models qualifies to be recognized over time, with the variable consideration (i.e., the actual usage payment) recognized based solely on usage during the service period.","section":"Business combination","block":178,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001493152-26-037914","form":"6-K","filedAt":"2026-08-14","reportDate":"2026-03-31","cik":"0002011458","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/2011458/000149315226037914/ex99-2.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/46ea7b4405496fa75ef5b65282048abb475d4c1ed2b08f8bad96510d1152995d.bin","sha256":"46ea7b4405496fa75ef5b65282048abb475d4c1ed2b08f8bad96510d1152995d"}},{"id":"221973b181948ce52e815da397a1443191636c8c6acdc58bbd34dce993359042","quote":"The Company follows the rules and guidance set out under ASC 606 when determining whether it is acting as a principal or an agent in the contract with its customers. The core principle of ASC 606 requires an entity to determine whether the nature of its promise is a performance obligation to provide the services itself (that is, the entity is a principal) or to arrange for those services to be provided by another party (that is, the entity is an agent). The following steps are applied to achieve that core principle:","context":"According to the agreement, the customers are required to settle the actual usage amounts on a quarterly basis and make payment within 60 days from the date signed on the usage confirmation letter. The customer adheres to the payment term and pays before the due date.","section":"Business combination","block":179,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001493152-26-037914","form":"6-K","filedAt":"2026-08-14","reportDate":"2026-03-31","cik":"0002011458","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/2011458/000149315226037914/ex99-2.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/46ea7b4405496fa75ef5b65282048abb475d4c1ed2b08f8bad96510d1152995d.bin","sha256":"46ea7b4405496fa75ef5b65282048abb475d4c1ed2b08f8bad96510d1152995d"}},{"id":"ac9cb5a98aa8109205b905d050a913e9c1711beba57970ff44a164bcfada83f4","quote":"Step 1: Identify the specified services to be provided to the customer.","context":"The Company follows the rules and guidance set out under ASC 606 when determining whether it is acting as a principal or an agent in the contract with its customers. The core principle of ASC 606 requires an entity to determine whether the nature of its promise is a performance obligation to provide the services itself (that is, the entity is a principal) or to arrange for those services to be provided by another party (that is, the entity is an agent). The following steps are applied to achieve that core principle:","section":"Business combination","block":180,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001493152-26-037914","form":"6-K","filedAt":"2026-08-14","reportDate":"2026-03-31","cik":"0002011458","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/2011458/000149315226037914/ex99-2.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/46ea7b4405496fa75ef5b65282048abb475d4c1ed2b08f8bad96510d1152995d.bin","sha256":"46ea7b4405496fa75ef5b65282048abb475d4c1ed2b08f8bad96510d1152995d"}},{"id":"93f4366544358cdeec75928ced2b5171754bc31feb3c415f350260aa7adeac06","quote":"Step 2: Assess whether it controls each specified service before that service is transferred to the customer.","context":"Step 1: Identify the specified services to be provided to the customer.","section":"Business combination","block":181,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001493152-26-037914","form":"6-K","filedAt":"2026-08-14","reportDate":"2026-03-31","cik":"0002011458","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/2011458/000149315226037914/ex99-2.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/46ea7b4405496fa75ef5b65282048abb475d4c1ed2b08f8bad96510d1152995d.bin","sha256":"46ea7b4405496fa75ef5b65282048abb475d4c1ed2b08f8bad96510d1152995d"}},{"id":"94471a13644ee84b71e14babd6d6c550c2dfb8009235906b67a133d48fba2456","quote":"Under the agreements the Company has with its customers, the Company has primary responsibility for providing algorithms and big data models. The fintech solution is fully owned and controlled by the Company, which has the authority to direct its use and derive substantially all of the remaining benefits from it. The Company also has full discretion to set the transaction prices in its agreements with customers. Furthermore, the Company is responsible for addressing and resolving any issues related to the models that are identified by customers. Based on these considerations, the Company concludes that it acts as a principal in its contracts with customers and recognizes revenue on a gross basis.","context":"Step 2: Assess whether it controls each specified service before that service is transferred to the customer.","section":"Business combination","block":182,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001493152-26-037914","form":"6-K","filedAt":"2026-08-14","reportDate":"2026-03-31","cik":"0002011458","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/2011458/000149315226037914/ex99-2.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/46ea7b4405496fa75ef5b65282048abb475d4c1ed2b08f8bad96510d1152995d.bin","sha256":"46ea7b4405496fa75ef5b65282048abb475d4c1ed2b08f8bad96510d1152995d"}},{"id":"2e074a2d38fd62519a261561f7322c343042ff0d17dafaa389c8dd6d2ea56577","quote":"The Company enters into distinct fintech services agreement with its customer to provide a blockchain system developed by a vendor for the customer’s use. As stipulated in the agreement, the Company will charge a one-time fixed services fee income for the system provided.","context":"Fintech service fees – blockchain","section":"Business combination","block":184,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001493152-26-037914","form":"6-K","filedAt":"2026-08-14","reportDate":"2026-03-31","cik":"0002011458","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/2011458/000149315226037914/ex99-2.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/46ea7b4405496fa75ef5b65282048abb475d4c1ed2b08f8bad96510d1152995d.bin","sha256":"46ea7b4405496fa75ef5b65282048abb475d4c1ed2b08f8bad96510d1152995d"}},{"id":"43d3bb08551c02e81966403d2f1a21f3a1ee7727133ece803c74687b71834805","quote":"The fintech service agreement related to the procurement of the blockchain system is distinct and is identified as one performance obligation. The Company is obligated to make available a blockchain system developed by a vendor for the customer’s use. The fintech services is considered to be distinct that Company promises to transfer and is therefore considered to be one single performance obligation under ASC 606-10-25-14.","context":"The Company enters into distinct fintech services agreement with its customer to provide a blockchain system developed by a vendor for the customer’s use. As stipulated in the agreement, the Company will charge a one-time fixed services fee income for the system provided.","section":"Business combination","block":185,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001493152-26-037914","form":"6-K","filedAt":"2026-08-14","reportDate":"2026-03-31","cik":"0002011458","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/2011458/000149315226037914/ex99-2.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/46ea7b4405496fa75ef5b65282048abb475d4c1ed2b08f8bad96510d1152995d.bin","sha256":"46ea7b4405496fa75ef5b65282048abb475d4c1ed2b08f8bad96510d1152995d"}},{"id":"9dfa5d60f515966d699c19fd9ab26875701622dc7c1c71bdc9f5cd93be703db1","quote":"For blockchain system procured by the Company, the customer does not simultaneously receive and consume the benefits as the services are rendered, i.e. the system would only be consumed by the customer once it is implemented and operational.","context":"The fintech service agreement related to the procurement of the blockchain system is distinct and is identified as one performance obligation. The Company is obligated to make available a blockchain system developed by a vendor for the customer’s use. The fintech services is considered to be distinct that Company promises to transfer and is therefore considered to be one single performance obligation under ASC 606-10-25-14.","section":"Business combination","block":186,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001493152-26-037914","form":"6-K","filedAt":"2026-08-14","reportDate":"2026-03-31","cik":"0002011458","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/2011458/000149315226037914/ex99-2.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/46ea7b4405496fa75ef5b65282048abb475d4c1ed2b08f8bad96510d1152995d.bin","sha256":"46ea7b4405496fa75ef5b65282048abb475d4c1ed2b08f8bad96510d1152995d"}},{"id":"d0f4aca106f5bb02ad516c0dad93088f0a5e03795766b385b87e832cc9708a74","quote":"The Company also does not create or enhance an asset that the customer controls as the performance obligation is simply to distribute the system for the customer use. No asset will be created by the Company as part of the performance obligation whilst the Company is simply to procure a blockchain model for the use of the customer. The customer would only be allowed the access to the system upon the product distribution and system implementation.","context":"For blockchain system procured by the Company, the customer does not simultaneously receive and consume the benefits as the services are rendered, i.e. the system would only be consumed by the customer once it is implemented and operational.","section":"Business combination","block":187,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001493152-26-037914","form":"6-K","filedAt":"2026-08-14","reportDate":"2026-03-31","cik":"0002011458","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/2011458/000149315226037914/ex99-2.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/46ea7b4405496fa75ef5b65282048abb475d4c1ed2b08f8bad96510d1152995d.bin","sha256":"46ea7b4405496fa75ef5b65282048abb475d4c1ed2b08f8bad96510d1152995d"}},{"id":"43ce0c286be4e9c1324c46b6acddb412b25b9cb6d64f0ac6ffc40afea2e918f0","quote":"The Company does not have an enforceable right to payment for performance completed to date. The services rendered by the Company are system procurement and implementation. The Company will only be entitled to fee upon the successful implementation of the system for the customer pursuant to the contracts without payment for performance completed to date.","context":"The Company also does not create or enhance an asset that the customer controls as the performance obligation is simply to distribute the system for the customer use. No asset will be created by the Company as part of the performance obligation whilst the Company is simply to procure a blockchain model for the use of the customer. The customer would only be allowed the access to the system upon the product distribution and system implementation.","section":"Business combination","block":188,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001493152-26-037914","form":"6-K","filedAt":"2026-08-14","reportDate":"2026-03-31","cik":"0002011458","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/2011458/000149315226037914/ex99-2.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/46ea7b4405496fa75ef5b65282048abb475d4c1ed2b08f8bad96510d1152995d.bin","sha256":"46ea7b4405496fa75ef5b65282048abb475d4c1ed2b08f8bad96510d1152995d"}},{"id":"5439b7ed9c67c35978cbacbc56a821648e53ba79112b79f7664db8e1510ef449","quote":"Because the revenue generated from procuring the blockchain system does not meet any of the criteria set out in ASC 606-10-25-27, the revenue from procuring the blockchain system does not qualify to be recognized over time but at a point in time.","context":"The Company does not have an enforceable right to payment for performance completed to date. The services rendered by the Company are system procurement and implementation. The Company will only be entitled to fee upon the successful implementation of the system for the customer pursuant to the contracts without payment for performance completed to date.","section":"Business combination","block":189,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001493152-26-037914","form":"6-K","filedAt":"2026-08-14","reportDate":"2026-03-31","cik":"0002011458","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/2011458/000149315226037914/ex99-2.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/46ea7b4405496fa75ef5b65282048abb475d4c1ed2b08f8bad96510d1152995d.bin","sha256":"46ea7b4405496fa75ef5b65282048abb475d4c1ed2b08f8bad96510d1152995d"}},{"id":"56e48ee0e03145128c13657ef788dc85962d8d7fabc6fabbfe738ebcc151634b","quote":"Revenue from providing the blockchain system to a customer is recognized at a point in time when the system is implemented and operational for the customer.","context":"Because the revenue generated from procuring the blockchain system does not meet any of the criteria set out in ASC 606-10-25-27, the revenue from procuring the blockchain system does not qualify to be recognized over time but at a point in time.","section":"Business combination","block":190,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001493152-26-037914","form":"6-K","filedAt":"2026-08-14","reportDate":"2026-03-31","cik":"0002011458","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/2011458/000149315226037914/ex99-2.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/46ea7b4405496fa75ef5b65282048abb475d4c1ed2b08f8bad96510d1152995d.bin","sha256":"46ea7b4405496fa75ef5b65282048abb475d4c1ed2b08f8bad96510d1152995d"}},{"id":"1b8c7cf14a72488e741a35f05c14aeeeaf42eea8b49450ef177cfc91b9affbdc","quote":"Under the agreement, it requires payment within 60 days following the implementation of system. The customer adheres to the payment term and pays before the due date.","context":"Revenue from providing the blockchain system to a customer is recognized at a point in t